# No Dev/Jargon Placeholders

Public UI copy is for customers. HelpNova is **not** a demo or sample website in visitor-facing text. When writing or editing visible copy, find sample/demo/dev wording and remove or rewrite it.

Replace or remove words and phrases such as: sample, demo, demonstration, concept website, draft policy, preset, placeholder, dummy, mock, local session, widget, slug, module, component, reducer, seed, demo-only, display-only, no AI model call, task IDs, and developer notes.

Write the replacement as clean, stable, conversion-focused English: short, specific, and useful to someone deciding to explore HelpNova. Keep the same meaning and the same UI control. If a badge or notice exists only to say “sample/demo,” delete the control so no empty space remains.

Do not claim a message was delivered, an account was created, an integration was connected, a payment was taken, or that a live AI model answered. Do not invent testimonials, measured savings, or customer outcomes.

Leave code, type names, file names, routes, and comments unchanged. Change only text a visitor can read.
